@startuml VerifiedEmailResetFlow
!include ../themes/dark-theme.puml
hide footbox

actor User
participant "Auth gRPC" as Auth
participant "Reset Orchestrator" as Reset
participant "VerifiedEmail Store" as EmailStore
participant "Reset Token Service" as TokenService
participant "Mail Provider" as Mail
participant "Audit Log" as Audit
participant "Database" as DB

User -> Auth: Request password reset
Auth -> Reset: startReset(email)
Reset -> EmailStore: find verified identity for email
alt #F3B6BE99 Unknown or unverified
    EmailStore --> Reset: none
    Reset --> Auth: enumeration-safe response
    Auth --> User: reset requested / not found
    Reset -> Audit: record reset_request_unknown
else #C7E8C999 Verified identity exists
    EmailStore --> Reset: verified user + email metadata
    Reset -> TokenService: issue single-use reset token
    TokenService --> Reset: short-lived token
    Reset -> Mail: send reset link or code
    Mail --> Reset: delivery outcome
    Reset -> DB: persist reset event and token hash
    Reset -> Audit: record reset_issued + delivery_result
    Auth --> User: reset email sent
end

User -> Auth: Submit reset token + new password
Auth -> Reset: completeReset(token, newPassword)
Reset -> TokenService: validate token and purpose
alt #F3B6BE99 Expired / replayed / invalid
    TokenService --> Reset: invalid
    Reset -> Audit: record reset_failed
    Reset --> Auth: INVALID_TOKEN or RESET_EXPIRED
    Auth --> User: reset failed
else #C7E8C999 Valid
    TokenService --> Reset: verified principal
    Reset -> DB: atomically store new hash, revoke prior token family
    Reset -> Audit: record reset_consumed
    Reset --> Auth: success
    Auth --> User: password reset complete
end
@enduml
